{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>I will blot out the human.</b> It does not say 'he was blotted out,' as it says 'let us make human' — because when He created him, the angels said, 'what is man that You remember him,' and they did not agree to create him. Therefore He did not take counsel from them to blot him out. But afterward, when He changed the appointed overseers, He took counsel from them to blot him out, as it is written: 'come, let us descend and confound their language.'" "<b>For I regret that I made them.</b> Since the evil of man had multiplied. But when they do the will of the Place, 'El is not a man that He should lie, nor a son of man that He should regret.' And likewise it says: 'I regret that I have made Saul king, for he has turned away from behind Me' — the turning away comes from them, as I explained above. <b>The series of Bereshit is completed.</b>"], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:03:09.074152261Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}